# Package manager: pnpm

Use pnpm (pinned in the root `package.json`) for every install and script. The lockfile is `pnpm-lock.yaml`.

- Workspace-wide scripts run from the root: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm format:check`.
- Package scripts go through their shortcut: `pnpm web <script>`, `pnpm mobile <script>`, `pnpm swarm <command>`.
- Add a dependency to the package that uses it: `pnpm --filter <package> add <dep>`.
- `tools/brand` is the one exception: it keeps its own npm lockfile and CI job.
